Literary reading, forms, and interpretation (@literary-reading-forms-and-interpretation: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_4CTQ8C4X2Q4CYPKQXDKQY4AJ6T
Literary study begins with attentive reading of particular works and the forms through which they create meaning. This material introduces narrative, poetry, drama, and the essay through voice, perspective, character, imagery, rhythm, structure, and ambiguity. Routes develop an interpretation from passages and explain how another reading might challenge it. Introduce terminology alongside its use and connect the work to philosophical questions and historical context without replacing the work itself with a summary.

**Parent:** [Literature](../Literature.lingua#r_68XTEFTFVR5ZPB68D6E1XK0SR3).
